Title: Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for tb-001: Is the data column sidecar inclusion proof correctly verified?
Severity: High
Property: PROP-W4B13-70
Bug Class: Cryptographic Proof Validation
Primary File: beacon-chain/core/peerdas/p2p_interface.go:VerifyDataColumnSidecarInclusionProof

ACTUAL CODE:
```go
func VerifyDataColumnSidecarInclusionProof(sidecar blocks.RODataColumn) error {
    if sidecar.SignedBlockHeader == nil || sidecar.SignedBlockHeader.Header == nil {
        return ErrNilBlockHeader
    }
    root := sidecar.SignedBlockHeader.Header.BodyRoot
    if len(root) != fieldparams.RootLength {
        return ErrBadRootLength
    }
    leaves := blocks.LeavesFromCommitments(sidecar.KzgCommitments)
    sparse, err := trie.GenerateTrieFromItems(leaves, fieldparams.LogMaxBlobCommitments)
    if err != nil { return errors.Wrap(err, "generate trie from items") }
    hashTreeRoot, err := sparse.HashTreeRoot()
    if err != nil { return errors.Wrap(err, "hash tree root") }

    verified := trie.VerifyMerkleProof(root, hashTreeRoot[:], kzgPosition, sidecar.KzgCommitmentsInclusionProof)
    if !verified { return ErrInvalidInclusionProof }
    return nil
}
```

Caller in data_column.go (SidecarInclusionProven):
```go
func (dv *RODataColumnsVerifier) SidecarInclusionProven() (err error) {
    if ok, err := dv.results.cached(RequireSidecarInclusionProven); ok {
        return err
    }
    defer dv.recordResult(RequireSidecarInclusionProven, &err)

    for _, dataColumn := range dv.dataColumns {
        k, keyErr := inclusionProofKey(dataColumn)
        if keyErr == nil {
            if _, ok := dv.ic.Get(k); ok {
                continue  // CACHE HIT: skip verification
            }
        } else {
            log.WithError(keyErr).Error("Failed to get inclusion proof key")
        }

        if err = peerdas.VerifyDataColumnSidecarInclusionProof(dataColumn); err != nil {
            return columnErrBuilder(ErrSidecarInclusionProofInvalid)
        }

        if keyErr == nil {
            dv.ic.Add(k, struct{}{})
        }
    }
    return nil
}
```

=== ITEM 5: CHK-0055 ===
Title: Does actor-p2p-peer relay only data column sidecars with valid inclusion proofs?
Severity: Medium
Property: PROP-W4B13-70
Bug Class: Gossip Validation Order
Primary File: beacon-chain/sync/validate_data_column.go:validateDataColumn

ACTUAL GOSSIP VALIDATION ORDER:
```go
func (s *Service) validateDataColumn(ctx context.Context, pid peer.ID, msg *pubsub.Message) (pubsub.ValidationResult, error) {
    // 1. ValidFields() - structural check
    // 2. CorrectSubnet() - subnet routing
    // 3. NotFromFutureSlot() - IGNORE (time check)
    // 4. SlotAboveFinalized() - IGNORE
    // 5. SidecarParentSeen() - IGNORE (async parent fetch if needed)
    // 6. SidecarParentValid() - REJECT
    // 7. ValidProposerSignature() - REJECT (ordering deviated from spec)
    // 8. SidecarParentSlotLower() - REJECT
    // 9. SidecarDescendsFromFinalized() - REJECT
    // 10. SidecarInclusionProven() - REJECT (inclusion proof)
    // 11. validateWithKzgBatchVerifier() - REJECT (KZG proofs)
    // 12. hasSeenDataColumnIndex() - IGNORE (dedup)
    // 13. SidecarProposerExpected() - REJECT
    // --> ValidationAccept
}
```

Note: SidecarInclusionProven is called BEFORE KZG batch verification (step 10 vs 11). The order matters for DoS prevention - an attacker could craft sidecars with valid inclusion proofs but invalid KZG proofs.

